  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "With the CMDA changes, a new \"Fedora Object Type\" (fType) was introduced: \"C\".  Now the set of possible fTypes includes \"O\" (data object), \"D\" (bdef object), \"M\" (bmech object), and \"C\" (content model object).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The fType attribute has always been a single-valued required attribute.  With the CMDA changes, this was turned into a repeating attribute of the DigitalObject class.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We need to decide whether we really want this, long-term.  Things to consider:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) How would it be specified in the FOXML or METS if multiple values were allowed (a delimited string, or multiple elements/attributes?)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "2) It is currently not possible to ingest an object that specifies it's of multiple Fedora Object types.  Schematron validation (foxml and mets) both catch this as an error.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "3) If it were possible, we don't have any tests that exercise this capability: none of the test/demo objects are of multiple types.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Things that would be particularly important to test include:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "How the resource index update behaves when an object is of two types.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "How the fieldsearch interface would behave.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "How the admin client indicates multiple types to the user.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "On the other hand, if we decide to back off of this \"multi-valued fType\" capability, the DigitalObject class and DOReader, etc., should be updated to use a simple getter/setter for this value.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
